{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8a1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0c8-2197-71f2-b37c-575c8ab978c8"},"sequence":683,"recorded_at":1780531400001361,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0ca-0724-70e1-8fef-0212e3a02c0f"},"task_id":"01a0b0ca-0724-70e1-8fef-0212e3a02c0f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0ca-0724-70e1-8fef-0212e3a02c0f","chunk":"Read text file `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1geqhj: implementation evidence\n2|\n3|Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec v0.5.0, commit\n4|`28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`, worked against the\n5|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md` headings named below (the v0.7.0\n6|adoption is byte-identical in these sections). Primary scope is\n7|Sections 4.B-4.D, 4.1-4.2, 5.2 Terminal Events, 7.A, and 13.1, plus\n8|the 2.4 profile authority the wrapper composes. This file records\n9|implementation evidence; per the Story contract the\n10|`internal/traceability` ownership registry is untouched in this\n11|first leaf — the Story's final leaf carries the registry bindings\n12|and re-pin. This package claims no public CLI delivery: no `ax`\n13|command exists in this tree.\n14|\n15|The wrapper validation core (`internal/axpane`) composes every\n16|check from a landed gate and re-implements none: owner epoch and\n17|fencing from `fencing` (`AuthorizeActivation`, `AuthorizeRestore`,\n18|the sealed `LeaseToken`, the parked vocabulary); materialization\n19|validity from `matjournal` (`Store.Get` with its grammar and\n20|cross-reference validation, plus the stated committed-phase rule)\n21|and checkpoint admission from `sessckpt` (`Get`, which re-attests\n22|through `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord` on every read) with the\n23|identity match in `Decide`; the effective persisted profile from\n24|`sessprofile` (`DecodeRecord`, `DecodeEvent`, `Derive`) with\n25|Section 7.7 mapping from `provhost` (`ResolveMapping`,\n26|`profile_mapping_unavailable`); provider identity from `provhost`\n27|(`CheckResumeTuple`, `VerifyIdentityBuild`,\n28|`VerifyIdentityDiscovery`, `CreateIdentity` in fixtures) with\n29|`resumesmoke` evidence (`VerifyRecord`) as a precondition input;\n30|backend identity from `terminalbackend` (`ParseManifest`,\n31|`ParseProbe`, `ParseEvidence`, `GenerationDigest`, `Reconcile`,\n32|`CapabilitiesForOperation` via `CheckOperation`, `CheckEntrypoint`,\n33|`AdmitProviderDescriptor`); configuration validity from `config`\n34|(`Load`); session, lease, and event durability from `sessrepo`\n35|(`GetRecord`, `ListEvents`, `ListSessions`, `fencing.Observe` over\n36|`ListLeases`, `AppendEvent`); refusal shapes from `axerror`\n37|(`NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable`, `NewTargetAuthMissing`).\n38|\n39|## Acceptance rows\n40|\n41|41 of 41 AC rows are driven at the production entries named below;\n42|0 of 41 are delivered as a public CLI surface, which is an explicit\n43|caller-integration bound (no `ax` command exists in this tree), not\n44|a gap in the assigned validation behavior. Process control, mesh\n45|transport, provider supervision, and backend operations belong to\n46|modeled callers and later leaves, which invoke these entries at\n47|every required boundary.\n48|\n49|| AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) | Evidence and bound |\n50|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n51|| Lower epoch parks or refuses | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_lower_epoch` | Driven: presented epoch 1 under a winning epoch 2 parks `stale_owner` with the winning lease. |\n52|| Same-epoch loser parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_same_epoch_loser` | Driven: the losing lease at the winning epoch parks `stale_owner`. |\n53|| Future epoch parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_future_epoch` | Driven: an epoch beyond the winner parks `restore_policy`. |\n54|| Foreign session refuses | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/refused_fencing_foreign_session` | Driven: a token for another session refuses `lease_conflict`. |\n55|| Expired grant refuses | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` → `sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry` | `TestDecideTable/refused_fencing_expired_grant` | Driven: a lapsed grant refuses `lease_conflict` on the launch entry. |\n56|| Malformed token refuses | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/refused_fencing_malformed_token` | Driven: epoch 0 refuses `invalid_arguments`. |\n57|| Absent winner parks without authority | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation`; `Run` skips emission | `TestDecideTable/parked_absent_winner`, `TestRunParkedWithoutWinnerSkipsEmission` | Driven: no winner parks `restore_policy` with an empty lease ID and authors no event, since `session.parked` requires a winning lease. |\n58|| Ambiguous ownership parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_ambiguous` | Driven: conflicting union observations park `restore_policy`. |\n59|| Unverified ownership parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_unverified`, `TestRunParkedEmits` | Driven: without a proving lease refresh the wrapper parks and authors the parked event under the winner. |\n60|| Failed handoff parks | `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` | `TestDecideTable/parked_failed_handoff` | Driven: a losing force lease parks `failed_handoff`, never activates. |\n61|| Remote interactive owner offers attach | `Decide` → `decideParked` + `terminalbackend.CheckOperation(\"attach\")` | `TestDecideTable/attach_remote_interactive` | Driven: a remote winning holder with an interactive terminal and an admitted attach capability offers `attach_remote` with no lease mutation. |\n62|| Remote owner otherwise offers takeover | `Decide` → `decideParked` | `TestDecideTable/takeover_offer_noninteractive`, `TestDecideTable/takeover_offer_attach_unproven`, `TestRunTakeoverOfferEmitsParked` | Driven: a non-interactive or attach-unproven remote owner offers `takeover_offer`, starts no runtime, and still authors the `remote_owner` parked event. |\n63|| Mode selects entry and capability row | `Decide` → `authorize` + `admitBackend` | `TestDecideRestoreRequiresRestoreCapability`, `TestDecideTable/launch_restore_committed_checkpoint` | Driven: restore mode gates through `AuthorizeRestore` and the `restore` row (a restore-admitting, create-denying backend launches); launch mode gates through `AuthorizeActivation` and `create`. |\n64|| Materialization validity gates local resume | `Decide` (journal arm); `Run` → `LoadMaterialization` | `TestDecideTable/parked_materialization_not_committed`, `TestDecideTable/parked_materialization_absent`, `TestRunRestoreCommitted`, `TestRunRestoreMaterializingParks` | Driven: a required journal must be admitted by the `matjournal` owner and committed (stated phase rule); staging or absence parks `restore_policy`. Fresh launch leaves the requirement unset (§13.1 runs before the journal commits). |\n65|| Checkpoint admission gates resume | `Decide` → `admitCheckpoint` → `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord`; `Run` → `LoadCheckpoint` | `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_inadmissible`, `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_absent`, `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_wrong_identity`, `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_flipped_digest` | Driven: a required checkpoint must attest through the `sessrepo` owner and match the required digest; garbage, absence, or identity drift parks `restore_policy`. |\n66|| Effective profile derived with source | `Decide` → `sessprofile.Derive`; `Run` → `LoadProfile` | `TestDecideProfileSourcePinsEvent`, `TestDecideYoloMapping` | Driven: the launch carries the newest authoritative `profile.changed` target with that event's digest as source (PROFILE-DIRECT-RESUME direction); creation-only chains carry the record value with null source. Corrupt derivation refuses `integrity_failure` (`TestDecideTable/refused_profile_derivation_corrupt`). |\n67|| Profile mapping resolved or refused | `Decide` → `provhost.ResolveMapping` | `TestDecideYoloMapping`, `TestDecideTable/refused_profile_mapping_unavailable` | Driven: the yolo launch carries the exact codex adapter flag; a Pi build off the pinned version refuses `profile_mapping_unavailable` per §2.4. The tuple gate precedes mapping so a tuple refusal keeps its own class. |\n68|| Resume tuple gate | `Decide` → `checkProviderIdentity` → `provhost.CheckResumeTuple` | `TestDecideTable/refused_provider_tuple_qwen` | Driven: a tuple outside the §8.4 direction refuses `invalid_config` with the landed detail. |\n69|| Identity bind to exact build | `Decide` → `provhost.VerifyIdentityBuild` | `TestDecideTable/refused_provider_identity_other_provider` | Driven: an identity minted for another provider (`CreateIdentity` fixture) refuses `invalid_config`; the probed version must equal the record version exactly. |\n70|| Discovery bind | `Decide` → `provhost.VerifyIdentityDiscovery` | `TestDecideTable/launch_discovery_bound`, `TestDecideTable/refused_discovery_native_mismatch`, `TestDecideTable/refused_discovery_root_outside`, `TestDecideTable/refused_discovery_empty_home` | Driven: a proof binding the identity's native ID under the §8.2 store root launches; native drift, an outside root, or an empty home refuse `invalid_config`. |\n71|| Provider-auth smoke precondition | `Decide` → `checkSmoke` → `resumesmoke.VerifyRecord` + `axerror.NewTargetAuthMissing` | `TestDecideTable/refused_smoke_failing_verdict`, `TestDecideTable/refused_smoke_absent`, `TestDecideTable/refused_smoke_wrong_build`, `TestDecideTypedRefusals/target_auth_missing_details`, `TestRunSmokeRequiredPasses` | Driven: a required smoke must verify, pass, and bind the exact probed build; failure, absence, or build drift refuses `target_auth_missing` with the typed §15.3 details. |\n72|| Backend identity admission | `Decide` → `admitBackend` → `terminalbackend.ParseManifest/ParseProbe/ParseEvidence/Reconcile` | `TestDecideLaunchPositive` | Driven: a real manifest/probe/RSA-signed-evidence universe reconciles and admits `headless_creation` for `create` (and `reboot_restoration` for `restore`, `local_attach` for `attach`). |\n73|| Mismatch fails before activation | `Decide` → `admitBackend` | `TestDecideTable/refused_backend_protocol_membership`, `TestDecideTable/refused_backend_generation_mismatch`, `TestDecideTable/refused_backend_evidence_expired`, `TestDecideTable/refused_backend_signature_untrusted` | Driven: protocol drift refuses `terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch`; generation drift refuses the more specific `terminal_backend_stale_generation`; expired evidence refuses; an untrusted signature refuses `terminal_backend_integrity_failure`. |\n74|| Only admitted rows authorize | `Decide` → `terminalbackend.CheckOperation` | `TestDecideTable/refused_backend_capability_unproven` | Driven: with no admitted capability conferring `create`, the wrapper refuses `terminal_backend_capability_unproven`. No capability map is invented: the `Reconcile` set is the only authority. |\n75|| Background caller without attested server | `Decide` → `checkRealm` → `axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable` | `TestDecideTable/refused_realm_background_no_server`, `TestDecideTypedRefusals/capability_unavailable_details`, `TestDecideTable/launch_background_attested_server` | Driven: a background caller with no attested server refuses `capability_unavailable` with typed realm/readiness details and never creates a server; an attested server launches. Incomplete typed details refuse `invalid_arguments` (`TestDecideTable/refused_realm_background_incomplete_details`). |\n76|| Cached evidence never authorizes | `Realm` struct (structural) | `TestRealmCarriesNoCachedEvidence` | Driven: the `Realm` input carries exactly caller, attested-server fact, and typed details — no member accepts a cached sentinel or `managername` observation, so neither can authorize resume through any input value. |\n77|| Bootstrap idempotency | `Store.Bind`, `Decide` (idempotency arm), `Run` | `TestDecideTable/refused_idempotency_mismatch`, `TestDecideTable/reattach_same_pair`, `TestBindIdenticalRetryReattaches`, `TestBindChangedOperationRefusesMismatch`, `TestBindConcurrentSameOperationReattaches`, `TestBindConcurrentChangedOperationRefuses`, `TestRunReattaches`, `TestRunConcurrentLaunchReattaches`, `TestRunIdempotencyMismatch` | Driven: a changed operation in the bootstrap window refuses `idempotency_mismatch`; an identical retry reattaches to the one recorded child (the stored receipt is authoritative); a concurrent same-operation commit reattaches while a changed-operation commit refuses. |\n78|| Status proves absence or the one child | `Store.Status` | `TestBindInstallsAndStatusProves`, `TestStatusSessionMismatchRefuses` | Driven: absence proves only when no binding exists; a receipt read under another session refuses even with a shared prefix. |\n79|| Unknown is not absent | `Store.Status`, `Run` | `TestStatusUnknownIsNotAbsent`, `TestRunTornBindingPropagates` | Driven: a torn receipt fails `Status` and propagates through `Run` with no decision — never absence, never a launch. |\n80|| Crash at the binding seam | `Store.Bind` + `Hooks` | `TestBindCrashChildSelfTerminates`, `TestBindHookAfterStageAbortsWithoutInstall`, `TestBindHookAfterInstallKeepsTheCommit` | Driven: a real SIGKILL after the no-replace commit leaves the complete binding and the identical retry reattaches; an aborted stage leaves absence the retry converges from; a post-commit hook error keeps the commit. |\n81|| No PID persisted | `Store.Bind` (closed receipt) | `TestBindingPersistsNoPID` | Driven: the stored bytes carry exactly the seven closed members — UUIDv7 instance plus opaque digest — and no PID/handle/socket/endpoint/token member. |\n82|| Stable entrypoint | `Decide` → `terminalbackend.CheckEntrypoint` | `TestDecideTable/refused_entrypoint_raw_provider` | Driven: a raw provider argv refuses `local_precondition_failed`; only `ax pane SESSION_ID` passes. |\n83|| §7.A descriptor supplied and admitted | `BuildDescriptor`, `Decide` → `terminalbackend.AdmitProviderDescriptor` | `TestDescriptorBuildAdmitRoundTrip`, `TestDescriptorMismatchRefuses`, `TestDescriptorGenerationBounds`, `TestDecideTable/refused_descriptor_generation_drift` | Driven: the wrapper supplies the closed descriptor (fresh UUIDv7 instance, never a PID) and admits it against the validated host-local binding before any launch effect — parse, match, then launch, with no caching across the check. Binding, version, and generation drift refuse; generation lengths 0 and 257 refuse while 256 admits. |\n84|| Fencing token passed separately | `Decide` (token projection) → `fencing.LeaseToken.Bind` | `TestDecideLaunchPositive`, `TestDecideForgedTokensRefuse`, `TestObserveLoadsWinningLease` | Driven: launch and reattach carry the sealed token minted by the passed gate, binding `quiesce`/`capture`/`materialize` to the winning triple; parked, refused, and offer decisions carry the zero token, which refuses every provider operation. |\n85|| `session.parked` authored under lease | `EmitParked` → `Emit` → `sessrepo.AppendEvent` | `TestEmitParkedRoundTrip`, `TestEmitParkedVocabularyLoop`, `TestRunParkedEmits`, `TestRunTakeoverOfferEmitsParked`, `TestEmitParkedRefusesNonParked` | Driven: parked and remote-offer decisions author the exact closed payload (all four reasons) under the winning lease with current chain linkage; launch and refused decisions emit nothing, and emission for a non-parked decision refuses. |\n86|| v4 terminal payloads | `TerminalCreatedPayload`, `ResumedPayload`, `Emit` | `TestTerminalCreatedPayload`, `TestResumedPayload`, `TestEmitTerminalV4RoundTrip` | Driven: both v4 payloads carry exactly the §5.2 members (opaque binding digest, backend identity, evidence IDs; checkpoint plus effective profile pair for resumed), append under schema 4.0.0, and read back; malformed members refuse. |\n87|| §13.1 step 3 durable entry before launch | `Run` → `Store.Bind` | `TestRunLaunchBinds`, `TestRunRestoreCommitted` | Driven: the bootstrap pair binds durably before the launch outcome returns; the binding names the launched instance. Provider launch itself is a later leaf (stated bound). |\n88|| §13.1 step 4 validated plan | `Decide` (mapping + descriptor + token) | `TestLaunchCarriesValidatedPlan` | Driven: every launch carries the resolved adapter mapping, the admitted descriptor, and the sealed token together — no partial plan. Provider argv/env supervision is a later leaf (stated bound). |\n89|| Configuration validated | `Run` → `ValidateConfig` → `config.Load`; `Decide` (config arm) | `TestDecideTable/refused_config_invalid`, `TestRunInvalidConfig` | Driven: a failing configuration load refuses `invalid_config` through the real loader. |\n90|| Session loaded | `Run` → `LoadSession`; `Decide` (session arm) | `TestDecideTable/refused_unknown_session`, `TestRunUnknownSession` | Driven: an unknown SESSION_ID refuses `invalid_arguments`; observation is skipped without a session. |\n91|| After-restore sequence 1-5 | `Decide` in restore mode | `TestDecideAfterRestoreSequence` | Driven: winning lease plus valid required materialization resumes; materializing, unverified, lease-absent, and remote-owner inputs park or offer per steps 3-5. The bounded mesh refresh of step 2 is the caller-reported `Verified` fact (stated bound: no network here). |\n92|| Arm precedence | `Decide` | `TestDecideArmPrecedence` | Driven: an all-faulted input refuses at the configuration arm first; peeling faults walks the documented order. |\n93|| Orchestrated effects | `Run` | `TestRunLaunchBinds`, `TestRunReattaches`, `TestRunParkedEmits`, `TestRunRefusedWritesNothing`, `TestObserveLoadsWinningLease` | Driven: exactly one effect per outcome — launch binds, reattach returns, parked/offers emit, refused writes nothing; ownership observes the real winning lease and authorizes through the fencing owner. |\n94|\n95|## Refusal and recovery coverage\n96|\n97|Every `N-` row is a genuine narrowing mutant: the gate stays\n98|present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it\n99|must reject, and the named behavioral test fails through the\n100|delivered harness (`internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py`, run as\n101|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3\n102|internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py`). Whole-arm deletes are not\n103|accepted as narrowing. The `C-` row is the applied harmless\n104|SURVIVED control. Verdicts below are from the evidence run\n105|(`mutants.log` in the producer evidence archive): 25 of 25 rows\n106|match, 24 KILLED plus the SURVIVED control.\n107|\n108|| Mutant | Weakening (one member admitted) | Killer test | Verdict |\n109|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n110|| N-config | Invalid config admitted on launch mode only | `TestDecideTable/refused_config_invalid` | KILLED |\n111|| N-mode | Empty mode admitted; other non-modes refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_empty_mode` | KILLED |\n112|| N-session | Unknown session admitted on launch mode only | `TestDecideTable/refused_unknown_session` | KILLED |\n113|| N-idempotency | Changed operation admitted on launch mode only | `TestDecideTable/refused_idempotency_mismatch` | KILLED |\n114|| N-caller | `batch` caller admitted; other non-callers refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_unknown_caller` | KILLED |\n115|| N-backend-op | Restore-mode callers admitted to the create row | `TestDecideRestoreRequiresRestoreCapability` | KILLED |\n116|| N-materialization | Staging journals admitted; absent and other phases park | `TestDecideTable/parked_materialization_not_committed` | KILLED |\n117|| N-checkpoint-absent | Absent checkpoints admitted; bad bytes still park | `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_absent` | KILLED |\n118|| N-checkpoint-prefix | Same-prefix digests admitted; full compare otherwise | `TestDecideTable/parked_checkpoint_flipped_digest` | KILLED |\n119|| N-identity-version | 0.147.0 identity mismatches admitted; other versions refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_provider_identity_other_provider` | KILLED |\n120|| N-discovery | Empty-home discovery admitted; other proofs verify | `TestDecideTable/refused_discovery_empty_home` | KILLED |\n121|| N-discovery | Empty-home discovery admitted; other proofs still verify | `TestDecideTable/refused_discovery_empty_home` | KILLED |\n122|| N-smoke-verdict | Failing verdicts admitted; gated/unsupported/unknown refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_smoke_failing_verdict` | KILLED |\n123|| N-smoke-version | Version drift admitted; provider/platform/arch still bind | `TestDecideTable/refused_smoke_wrong_build` | KILLED |\n124|| N-smoke-mode | Required smoke skipped on launch only | `TestDecideTable/refused_smoke_absent` | KILLED |\n125|| N-profile-derive | Corrupt derivation admitted for codex (wrong class surfaces) | `TestDecideTable/refused_profile_derivation_corrupt` | KILLED |\n126|| N-mapping | Standard mapping gaps admitted; yolo gaps refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_profile_mapping_unavailable` | KILLED |\n127|| N-realm | Broker-running background callers admitted; other states refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_realm_background_no_server` | KILLED |\n128|| N-entrypoint | Two-element argv admitted; other arities refuse | `TestDecideTable/refused_entrypoint_raw_provider` | KILLED |\n129|| N-descriptor | Launch-mode descriptor mismatch admitted; restore refuses | `TestDecideTable/refused_descriptor_generation_drift` | KILLED |\n130|| N-attach | Remote attach without the capability admitted | `TestDecideTable/takeover_offer_attach_unproven` | KILLED |\n131|| N-reattach | Launch selected over reattach on launch mode only | `TestDecideTable/reattach_same_pair` | KILLED |\n132|| N-binding-prefix | Same-prefix changed operations admitted at the race | `TestBindConcurrentChangedOperationRefuses` | KILLED |\n133|| N-binding-session | Same-prefix foreign sessions admitted at status | `TestStatusSessionMismatchRefuses` | KILLED |\n134|| N-parked-reason | Five-letter reasons admitted; vocabulary otherwise closed | `TestParkedPayloadVocabulary` | KILLED |\n135|| C-doc-comment | Comment-only control edit | `TestRealmCarriesNoCachedEvidence` | SURVIVED |\n136|\n137|No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: this package\n138|contains no gate that inspects source text (the `Realm` field\n139|enumeration runs through reflection over the compiled type, not\n140|source), so the additional behavioral-suite mutant the evidence\n141|contract names for such gates has no target here. The standalone\n142|`CheckResumeTuple` call in `checkProviderIdentity` is fail-fast\n143|ordering over the same gate `VerifyIdentityBuild` enforces\n144|internally, so weakening it alone is unobservable by construction;\n145|the N-identity-version mutant covers the provider-identity gate as\n146|a whole. The fencing entry selection (`AuthorizeRestore` vs\n147|`AuthorizeActivation`) shares one launch-class core in the\n148|`fencing` owner, so no behavioral delta exists to mutate; the\n149|mode-selected backend capability row carries the mode mutant\n150|(N-backend-op).\n151|\n152|## Crash and idempotency evidence\n153|\n154|The bootstrap binding is the only durable write. It installs under\n155|the landed discipline: same-directory staging, 0600, fsync, atomic\n156|link as the no-replace commit, staging cleanup, directory fsync\n157|(skipped, never faked, on Windows). Readers see absence or the\n158|complete receipt, never a torn prefix. Crash hooks arm both\n159|boundaries (`AfterStage` before the commit, `AfterInstall` after\n160|it); the real-kill test (`TestBindCrashChildSelfTerminates`)\n161|SIGKILLs the child between commit and directory sync and proves\n162|the complete binding plus a converging identical retry. Parked\n163|events append through the `sessrepo` owner, whose own crash\n164|evidence stays with that package; this leaf proves linkage and\n165|round-trip only.\n166|\n167|## Stated bounds\n168|\n169|- No `ax` CLI surface, no tmux/ConPTY process control, no provider\n170|  process supervision, no mesh transport, and no GUI/Keychain\n171|  broker live here. Those are modeled callers (their facts arrive\n172|  as `Decide` inputs) and later leaves.\n173|- The bounded mesh lease refresh (after-restore step 2) is the\n174|  caller-reported `Verified` fact, not a network call.\n175|- Signature verification is caller-supplied through\n176|  `terminalbackend.SignatureVerifier`; tests authenticate through\n177|  a generated RSA key.\n178|- Backend liveness (`terminal_backend_unavailable` at the\n179|  operation call site) belongs to the later backend-operation\n180|  leaf: no backend operation exists here, so no availability rule\n181|  is invented.\n182|- The host-local `InstanceBinding` the descriptor must match\n183|  arrives from the modeled backend caller; the wrapper proves\n184|  document-to-binding consistency and never mints backend\n185|  bindings.\n186|- The committed-phase rule for a required materialization is the\n187|  wrapper's stated reading of after-restore step 3 (\"the required\n188|  materialization is valid\").\n189|- Invalid materialization or checkpoint on an otherwise winning\n190|  local owner parks `restore_policy` per the literal step-5\n191|  reading (\"enter parked without launching the provider in all\n192|  other cases\"), with the blocking cause in the decision detail.\n193|- Unknown SESSION_ID refuses `invalid_arguments`: the call names\n194|  no logical session. No `unknown_session` wire code is minted.","final_result":true}}}
