{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cae3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0c8-2197-71f2-b37c-575c8ab978c8"},"sequence":972,"recorded_at":1780531400001939,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3"},"call_id":"call_01a0b0cc0363751e9d6630ee9a90a062","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-21-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n '270,340p' internal/axerror/details.go\\necho \\\"===spec 4.C / 4.2 need===\\\"\\nls internal/specdoc/ 2>&1\\ngrep -n \\\"credential_capable\\\\|headless_creation.*non-interactive\\\\|bootstrap window\\\\|bootstrap_operation_id.*session_id\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md | head -n 40\",\n  \"description\": \"Read realm details and spec excerpts\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"}\\n\\n// RealmEvidence is the exact typed detail set Section 15.3 requires when\\n// broker, tmux server generation, or functional-sentinel evidence is missing or\\n// unsafe: \\\"capability_unavailable with typed details containing capability,\\n// caller_realm, broker_state, tmux_server_generation, and remediation\\\".\\n//\\n// tmux_server_generation is carried here on that clause's explicit instruction.\\n// The Section 16.2 exclusion of backend generations governs manifests and\\n// bundles generated by ax, and the more specific clause licenses this one\\n// diagnostic field.\\ntype RealmEvidence struct {\\n\\tCapability           string\\n\\tCallerRealm          string\\n\\tBrokerState          string\\n\\tTmuxServerGeneration string\\n\\tRemediation          string\\n}\\n\\n// Details renders the typed set. Every field is required, because a caller that\\n// omits one has not produced the typed details the clause names.\\nfunc (evidence RealmEvidence) Details() (Details, error) {\\n\\treturn requiredTypedDetails(map[string]string{\\n\\t\\t\\\"capability\\\":             evidence.Capability,\\n\\t\\t\\\"caller_realm\\\":           evidence.CallerRealm,\\n\\t\\t\\\"broker_state\\\":           evidence.BrokerState,\\n\\t\\t\\\"tmux_server_generation\\\": evidence.TmuxServerGeneration,\\n\\t\\t\\\"remediation\\\":            evidence.Remediation,\\n\\t})\\n}\\n\\n// TargetAuth is the exact typed detail set Section 15.3 requires for\\n// target_auth_missing: \\\"typed provider_id, provider_build, macos_version,\\n// tmux_server_generation, and remediation\\\".\\ntype TargetAuth struct {\\n\\tProviderID           string\\n\\tProviderBuild        string\\n\\tMacOSVersion         string\\n\\tTmuxServerGeneration string\\n\\tRemediation          string\\n}\\n\\n// Details renders the typed set. Every field is required.\\nfunc (target TargetAuth) Details() (Details, error) {\\n\\treturn requiredTypedDetails(map[string]string{\\n\\t\\t\\\"provider_id\\\":            target.ProviderID,\\n\\t\\t\\\"provider_build\\\":         target.ProviderBuild,\\n\\t\\t\\\"macos_version\\\":          target.MacOSVersion,\\n\\t\\t\\\"tmux_server_generation\\\": target.TmuxServerGeneration,\\n\\t\\t\\\"remediation\\\":            target.Remediation,\\n\\t})\\n}\\n\\n// targetAuthMissingKeys is the presence requirement New enforces for\\n// target_auth_missing, so the generic constructor cannot emit that code with a\\n// weaker detail set than the typed constructor produces.\\nvar targetAuthMissingKeys = []string{\\n\\t\\\"macos_version\\\",\\n\\t\\\"provider_build\\\",\\n\\t\\\"provider_id\\\",\\n\\t\\\"remediation\\\",\\n\\t\\\"tmux_server_generation\\\",\\n}\\n\\nfunc requiredTypedDetails(fields map[string]string) (Details, error) {\\n\\tdetails := make(Details, len(fields))\\n\\tfor _, key := range sortedKeys(fields) {\\n\\t\\tif fields[key] == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\\\"%w: typed detail %q is required and must not be empty\\\", ErrInvalidDetails, key)\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tdetails[key] = fields[key]\\n===spec 4.C / 4.2 need===\\nembed_reach_test.go\\nSPEC.md\\nSPEC.v0.6.0.md\\nspecdoc_test.go\\nspecdoc.go\\nspecdoc060_test.go\\n1184:| <code>create</code> | <code>absent|stopped</code> → <code>active</code> when interactive, otherwise <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_started</code> and optionally <code>attach_client_created</code> | <code>create</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \\\"/\\\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before <code>wrapper_started</code>; identical retry replays it; uncertainty requires <code>status</code>; binding plus capability/credential evidence | <code>headless_creation</code> when non-interactive; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when provider credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\\n1191:| <code>restore</code> | <code>absent|stopped|unavailable</code> → <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_restored</code> | <code>restore</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \\\"/\\\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before restore; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; prior binding, Checkpoint, new binding, capability/credential evidence | <code>reboot_restoration</code>; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\\n1196:a changed operation in the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\\n1234:| <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> | Exact instance passes AX sentinel and provider-auth smoke without UI. | true | <code>create,restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,credential_sentinel,provider_auth_smoke,runtime_probe</code> |\\n1262:| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\\n1263:| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\\n1264:| <code>provider_build</code> | string[1..256]|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\\n1265:| <code>sentinel_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\\n1266:| <code>provider_auth_smoke_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\\n1378:the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. After a lost result,\\n9044:<em>bootstrap window</em>. The epoch-1 lease is authoritative with\\n9153:The task-board launch remains in the same bootstrap window until step 7. The\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6128,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1532,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
