{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd7b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0c8-2197-71f2-b37c-575c8ab978c8"},"sequence":1304,"recorded_at":1780531400002603,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0cf-5b37-79b3-b484-042f2f7d3582"},"task_id":"01a0b0cf-5b37-79b3-b484-042f2f7d3582","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0cf-5b37-79b3-b484-042f2f7d3582","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-33-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"axpane\\\\|cached sentinel\\\\|managername\\\\|AttestedServer\\\" README.md | head -n 30\\necho \\\"===LOGBOOK head===\\\"\\nhead -n 60 LOGBOOK.md\\necho \\\"===results head===\\\"\\nhead -n 100 /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-1geqhj/TASK-260830-1geqhj_results.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check README and logbook\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"2141:[`internal/axpane`](internal/axpane) implements the validation core of the\\n2163:sentinel or `managername` observation can authorize resume.\\n2168:go test ./internal/axpane -count=1\\n2169:go test ./internal/axpane -cover -count=1\\n2176:PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py\\n2186:[the task evidence map](internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n===LOGBOOK head===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1geqhj — ax pane enforcement wrapper validation core (first leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/axpane` — the pure `Decide` core (`launch|reattach|attach_remote|takeover_offer|parked|refused`), the `Run` orchestration over real stores, the durable bootstrap `(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)` binding store, §5.2 event authorship, and the §7.A descriptor builder. Every check composes a landed gate (`fencing`, `matjournal`, `sessckpt`/`sessrepo`, `sessprofile`, `provhost`, `resumesmoke`, `terminalbackend`, `config`, `axerror`); nothing is re-implemented. First leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\\n- F1: `fencing` launch entries refuse — not park — foreign sessions, malformed tokens, and lapsed grants, so the wrapper's `refused(lease_conflict)` rows for foreign/expired inputs compose directly; only remote/ambiguous/unverified/absent/stale ownership parks. Remote parks resolve locally to `attach_remote` (interactive + attach admitted) or `takeover_offer`, and both offers still author `session.parked` with `remote_owner`.\\n- F2: the tuple gate must precede profile mapping in arm order: `ResolveMapping` re-checks the tuple internally, so mapping-first would wear tuple refusals as `profile_mapping_unavailable`. The standalone `CheckResumeTuple` call stays as fail-fast ordering; weakening it alone is unobservable (defense in depth, stated in TRACEABILITY.md).\\n- F3: `terminalbackend.Reconcile` maps generation drift to the more specific `terminal_backend_stale_generation` (not the generic mismatch), and `create` is conferred by both `durable_disconnect` and `headless_creation` — the unproven vector must deny both. `sessckpt.Get` re-attests through `sessrepo` on every read, so checkpoint admission composes through the read path.\\n- F4: `Bind` is linearizable on the commit race via link-EEXIST re-read (same operation reattaches to the winner, changed operation refuses); the `AfterStage` hook plays the concurrent winner deterministically in tests. The store stamps `created_at` itself — scalar timestamps require ≥3 fractional digits, so `time.RFC3339Nano` (which omits trailing zeros) is not a valid stamp.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 24 narrowing mutants, all KILLED by named tests through `internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py`, plus the applied harmless SURVIVED control (25/25 rows match; per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits in the outcome tar). No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\\n- AC: 41 of 41 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via the no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n- F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\n- F2 (MEASURED BOUND): an idle stream with zero traffic does NOT self-close within one second of revocation — `serveLoop` carries no background watchdog. The next dispatch fences in milliseconds and `WatchGeneration` reports the commit; recorded as a stated bound with log evidence, not a pass. Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes likewise bounded.\\n- F3: `os/exec.Cmd.Wait` called twice hangs the second caller forever — test cleanup consumes one `Wait` channel. The 8 MiB line cap is enforced twice (framing + decode), so the oversize mutant weakens both layers in one multi-file probe (harness extended for `(file, old, new)` triples). The Structured Error schema URN is `urn:ax:schema:error`; a drift vector with the wrong URN passed for the wrong reason until the mutant survived and exposed it.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 9 new narrowing probes, all killed by named `TestHostile*` vectors (same-family ALPN, dual-layer oversize, client rebind, rpc-contracts, error-version drift, truncated-dispatch ignore, snapshot integrity, correlation, static nonce); pre-existing 26 probes re-run green (neutral passed, client-cache documented SURVIVED). Per-plant logs/tables in the outcome tar.\\n- TRACEABILITY: `AC-HOST-001` registered over 20 suite tests; new `unevidenced` bindings for 11.10.1–11.10.4 + 16.1 with honest gaps (executed lanes vs stated bounds); 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed; 11.10.5 stays unowned by design (no policy reader); digest re-pinned `e327bb08...`; report 102 cases / 61 bindings / 8 unowned / 17/487 clauses; README figures + tracecheck pins updated.\\n- AC: 7 of 7 hostile rows + 13 of 13 executed AC-HOST-001 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed. NOTE: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` replay against `origin/main e4e3e88` fails on a LOGBOOK.md rebase conflict (missing replay resolution) — orchestrator-side integration issue, worktree untouched at `244a7dc`.\\n- 2026-09-17 rev3 on `fc67abd`: pin `d3eca906…`, report 132 cases / 65 bindings / 7 unowned / 49 of 535 clauses; harness denominator 24 prior + 9 new; refresh-candidate completed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2atgj4 — property-test the ownership reducer (final leaf)\\n\\n- SCOPE: executable proofs of the four story-pinned ownership invariants\\n  (union-order independence, loser preservation, clock non-authority,\\n  zero duplicate authorized owners) over `sessstate.Reduce`/`Compare`,\\n  `sessrepo.WinningLease`/`ListLeases`, and `fencing.Authorize*`\\n  (Sections 2.2, 5.3, 13.6-13.10, v0.6.0). Final leaf of\\n  STORY-260830-1oqfec; carries the story-close traceability,\\n  README, and registry re-pin items.\\n- DEFECT (RED-first): `resolveWinner` reported each losing union lease\\n  against the transient arrival-order winner, so a loser's\\n  divergent-history evidence — even its presence — depended on union\\n  order (witness: `{R@1, A@1}` on an empty chain reports the loss in\\n  one arrival order and drops it in the other). FIX: two-pass\\n  resolution — select the greatest tuple first, then report every\\n  entry below it in ascending tuple order naming the final winner,\\n  with the off-chain flag recomputed from the final winner. All\\n  landed union assertions were order-free, so only the refusal-census\\n  line pins moved (sessstate.go:924/927 to :929/:932).\\n- GENERATORS: closed small alphabet, hand-written (no new dependency):\\n  exhaustive multisets of size 0..3 with all permutations and all\\n  ordered 2-partitions over three chain shapes, all `Compare`\\n  pairs/triples against an independent builtin-operator oracle, all\\n  reason sequences of length 0..2, the full presenter/observation/\\n  operation gate table, plus seeded-random union multisets (seed\\n  260830) and reason sequences (seed 260831) with recorded counts.\\n- MUTANTS (`internal/sessstate/testdata/mutate_properties.py`): 8\\n  narrowing plants (inverted tie-break, first-arrival evidence\\n  target, dropped same-/lower-epoch losers, clock-consulting\\n  creation and expiry, admitted same-epoch loser, admitted remote\\n  holder), each KILLED by its named property; applied harmless\\n  control SURVIVED; not-applied and compile-failure controls\\n  classified separately. The expiry plant is invisible to the landed\\n  suite (all-2026 fixtures) and only the translation property kills\\n===results head===\\n# TASK-260830-1geqhj results — ax pane enforcement wrapper\\n\\nStatus: ready for review (producer handoff; candidate UNCOMMITTED in the\\nStory worktree on `task-board/story/STORY-260830-ptxkqe`).\\n\\n## Deliverable\\n\\n`internal/axpane`: the validation core of the `ax pane SESSION_ID`\\nenforcement wrapper. The pure core `Decide` returns exactly one of\\n`launch|reattach|attach_remote|takeover_offer|parked(reason)|refused(class)`;\\n`Run` orchestrates the adapters over the real durable stores and applies\\nexactly the authorized effect; the bootstrap `(session_id,\\nbootstrap_operation_id)` store binds the one recorded wrapper/child under\\nthe no-replace + fsync discipline with crash hooks; §5.2 events author\\nthrough `sessrepo.AppendEvent` under the current lease; the §7.A descriptor\\nbuilder supplies the provider binding context.\\n\\nEvery check composes a landed gate (`fencing`, `matjournal`,\\n`sessckpt`/`sessrepo`, `sessprofile`, `provhost`, `resumesmoke`,\\n`terminalbackend`, `config`, `axerror`); nothing is re-implemented.\\n`internal/traceability` is untouched per the Story contract (the final leaf\\nre-pins); clause coverage lives in `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md` and the\\nconformance matrix.\\n\\n## AC coverage: 41 of 41 rows driven\\n\\nEvery command, message, state, and refusal in the AC is driven through a\\nproduction entry by a named committed test. Ratio: **41 of 41**.\\nProduction call sites per row are in the conformance matrix\\n(`TASK-260830-1geqhj_conformance-matrix.md`) and\\n`internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`. Headline rows:\\n\\n- Owner epoch / fencing: lower, losing, future, foreign, expired, malformed,\\n  absent, ambiguous, unverified, failed-handoff, remote (attach/takeover),\\n  mode-selected entry — via `Decide` → `fencing.AuthorizeActivation` /\\n  `AuthorizeRestore`.\\n- Materialization (required + committed) and checkpoint (required + attested\\n  + identity) — via `Decide` + `LoadMaterialization` / `LoadCheckpoint`.\\n- Effective profile + source, `profile_mapping_unavailable` — via `Decide` →\\n  `sessprofile.Derive` / `provhost.ResolveMapping`.\\n- Resume tuple, identity bind, discovery bind, smoke precondition with typed\\n  `target_auth_missing` — via `Decide` → `provhost.*` / `resumesmoke.*`.\\n- Backend identity (`Reconcile`), closed capabilities (`CheckOperation`),\\n  entrypoint, descriptor (`AdmitProviderDescriptor`) — via `Decide`.\\n- Background caller `capability_unavailable` with typed realm details;\\n  cached sentinel/`managername` structurally unauthorizing — via `Decide`.\\n- Bootstrap idempotency (same reattach, changed mismatch, commit race),\\n  status-proves-absence, real-kill crash seam, no-PID receipt — via\\n  `Store.Bind` / `Store.Status` / `Run`.\\n- `session.parked` (all four reasons, incl. offers), v4 `terminal.created` /\\n  `session.resumed` — via `EmitParked` / `Emit` / payload builders.\\n- After-restore steps 1-5, arm precedence, orchestrated effects — via\\n  `Decide` / `Run`.\\n\\n## Validation (this worktree, this session)\\n\\n- `go test ./internal/axpane -count=1` — exit 0 (full package suite).\\n- `go test ./internal/axpane -cover -count=1` — exit 0 (see coverage log).\\n- `go test ./... -count=1` — exit 0, 38 packages ok, no FAIL.\\n- `go test ./... -race -count=1` — exit 1 SOLELY on\\n  `internal/sessquery` hitting the default 10m `go test` timeout\\n  (37/38 packages ok, including `internal/axpane` in ~8s; no DATA\\n  RACE, no individual test failure anywhere). Reran in isolation:\\n  `go test ./internal/sessquery/ -race -count=1 -timeout 20m` —\\n  exit 0 in 552s. The suite is pre-existing slow under race (it\\n  needs ~9.2 minutes); my change cannot reach it (new package,\\n  zero importers; `sessquery` reads neither README nor LOGBOOK).\\n  Recorded honestly as a failing-as-configured gate with the\\n  isolation evidence attached (`sessquery-rerun.log`,\\n  `sessquery-long.log`).\\n- `go test ./internal/axpane/ -race -count=1` — exit 0.\\n- `go test ./internal/axpane/ -cover -count=1` — exit 0, 81.7%.\\n- `go test ./... -cover -count=1` — exit 0 (see cover log).\\n- `go build`, `go vet`, `gofmt` check, `GOOS=linux`/`windows` builds,\\n  JSON census, `git diff --check` — all exit 0.\\n- `tracecheck` — exit 0 (no registry change, as required for a first leaf).\\n- `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` —\\n  exit 0.\\n- 14/14 fuzz gates (`-fuzztime=100x`) — exit 0.\\n- `task-board validate` — exit 0 (187 pre-existing MISSING_ACTIVITY\\n  warnings on other items, none on this task or story).\\n- Mutant harness: 25/25 rows match — 24 narrowing mutants KILLED plus the\\n  applied harmless SURVIVED control (`mutants.log` with per-plant raw logs\\n  and subprocess exits).\\n\\n## Crash / idempotency evidence\\n\\n- Real-kill test `TestBindCrashChildSelfTerminates` (SIGKILL after the\\n  no-replace commit, before directory sync): the complete binding survives\\n  and the identical retry reattaches — no torn prefix, no second child.\\n- Hook tests pin both boundaries (aborted stage → absence + converging\\n  retry; post-commit hook error → commit stands + reattach).\\n- Commit-race tests pin linearizability (same-operation loser reattaches,\\n  changed-operation loser refuses `idempotency_mismatch`).\\n- Parked events append through the `sessrepo` owner (linkage + round-trip\\n  proven here; the owner's own crash evidence stays with that package).\\n\\n## Files (all UNCOMMITTED, candidate snapshot)\\n\\n- `internal/axpane/doc.go`, `decide.go`, `errors.go`, `binding.go`,\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 14339,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3585,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
