{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ce95","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0c8-2197-71f2-b37c-575c8ab978c8"},"sequence":1445,"recorded_at":1780531400002885,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0d0-3fdb-7372-b479-6f0086c29ee8"},"task_id":"01a0b0d0-3fdb-7372-b479-6f0086c29ee8","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0d0-3fdb-7372-b479-6f0086c29ee8","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 95-112\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-// Realm carries the §4.2 caller realm and broker readiness the\n-// background-caller arm decides over. There is deliberately no member\n-// for a cached sentinel result or a managername observation: neither\n-// authorizes resume, so neither is an input.\n-type Realm struct {\n-\t// Caller is CallerForeground or CallerBackground.\n-\tCaller string\n-\t// AttestedServer reports an already-running authenticated Aqua\n-\t// broker with its attested AX tmux server.\n-\tAttestedServer bool\n-\t// BrokerState, ServerGeneration, and Remediation are the typed\n-\t// realm/readiness details the capability_unavailable refusal\n-\t// carries. They are required: an empty member refuses\n-\t// invalid_arguments instead of emitting an untyped refusal.\n-\tBrokerState      string\n-\tServerGeneration string\n-\tRemediation      string\n-}\n+// Realm carries the §4.2 caller realm and broker readiness the\n+// background-caller arm decides over. There is deliberately no member\n+// for a cached sentinel result, a managername observation, or any\n+// attested-server boolean: none authorizes resume, so none is an\n+// input. A background caller authorizes only through the admitted\n+// credential_capable_execution_realm Capability Evidence row bound to\n+// the exact host binding, probed provider build, and current\n+// generation (§4.2, §4.D); the bare boolean previously carried here\n+// never authorizes and is removed.\n+type Realm struct {\n+\t// Caller is CallerForeground or CallerBackground.\n+\tCaller string\n+\t// BrokerState, ServerGeneration, and Remediation are the typed\n+\t// realm/readiness details the capability_unavailable refusal\n+\t// carries. They are required: an empty member refuses\n+\t// invalid_arguments instead of emitting an untyped refusal.\n+\t// ServerGeneration must equal the current AX-known raw\n+\t// generation the backend admission binds to; a stale generation\n+\t// refuses capability_unavailable, never launches.\n+\tBrokerState      string\n+\tServerGeneration string\n+\tRemediation      string\n+}\n+\n+// Closed capability names the wrapper's conditional arms evaluate.\n+// They repeat the §4.D registry rows the backend admission proves;\n+// the wrapper invents no capability.\n+const (\n+\t// credentialRealmCapability is the §4.D row a background caller\n+\t// must hold: the exact-instance sentinel plus provider-auth\n+\t// smoke bound to the terminal binding, provider build,\n+\t// generation digest, OS version, and expiry.\n+\tcredentialRealmCapability = \"credential_capable_execution_realm\"\n+\t// headlessCreationCapability is the §4.C create-row conditional\n+\t// a non-interactive create must hold.\n+\theadlessCreationCapability = \"headless_creation\"\n+)\n","final_result":true}}}
