{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e097","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0c8-2197-71f2-b37c-575c8ab978c8"},"sequence":3750,"recorded_at":1780531400007495,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0e2-891b-7b40-83ce-85c3bd9d6da2"},"task_id":"01a0b0e2-891b-7b40-83ce-85c3bd9d6da2","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0e2-891b-7b40-83ce-85c3bd9d6da2","chunk":"Read text file `internal/axpane/doc.go`.\n1|// Package axpane implements the validation core of the\n2|// `ax pane SESSION_ID` enforcement wrapper: the decision every managed\n3|// pane runs before launching, reattaching, offering, parking, or\n4|// refusing a provider.\n5|//\n6|// Normative scope: AX v0.6.0 Section 4.B (Terminal Backend\n7|// Manifest/Probe identity through the landed terminalbackend registry\n8|// and contract), Section 4.C/4.1/4.2 (the wrapper rule: validate\n9|// configuration, load the logical session, synchronize known lease\n10|// records when possible, compare the local fencing token before\n11|// launching a provider, park safely when ownership is remote,\n12|// ambiguous, or unverified; the after-restore sequence 1-5; terminal\n13|// creation and the wrapper's first child start idempotent on\n14|// (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id); no credential-dependent tmux\n15|// server creation from a background caller; a cached sentinel or\n16|// managername observation never authorizes resume), Section 4.D\n17|// (closed capabilities and evidence: only the exact admitted\n18|// capability rows authorize an action), Section 5.2 Terminal Events\n19|// (session.parked with its reason vocabulary, terminal.created and\n20|// session.resumed v4 terminal binding/evidence payloads), Section 7.A\n21|// (Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding descriptor),\n22|// and Section 13.1 Direct-session launch steps 3-4 (durable terminal\n23|// entry with the bootstrap operation ID, then provider launch with\n24|// its validated argv/env plan).\n25|//\n26|// Division of authority (no second model): every check is composed\n27|// from a landed gate, never re-implemented. Owner epoch and fencing\n28|// come from internal/fencing (AuthorizeActivation, AuthorizeRestore,\n29|// AuthorizeInput, the sealed LeaseToken projection, the parked\n30|// vocabulary); materialization validity from internal/matjournal\n31|// (Store.Get with its grammar and cross-reference validation plus\n32|// the committed-phase rule this package states) and checkpoint\n33|// admission from internal/sessckpt with internal/sessrepo attestation;\n34|// the effective persisted profile from internal/sessprofile\n35|// (Projector/Derive) with Section 7.7 mapping refusals from\n36|// internal/provhost (ResolveMapping, profile_mapping_unavailable);\n37|// provider identity from internal/provhost (CheckResumeTuple,\n38|// VerifyIdentityBuild, VerifyIdentityDiscovery) with\n39|// internal/resumesmoke evidence (VerifyRecord) as a precondition\n40|// input; backend identity from internal/terminalbackend\n41|// (ParseManifest, ParseProbe, ParseEvidence, GenerationDigest,\n42|// Reconcile, CapabilitiesForOperation, CheckOperation,\n43|// CheckEntrypoint, AdmitProviderDescriptor); configuration validity\n44|// from internal/config (Load); session, lease, and event durability\n45|// from internal/sessrepo (GetRecord, ListEvents, Observe/WinningLease,\n46|// AppendEvent); refusal shapes from internal/axerror\n47|// (NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable for the background-caller\n48|// capability_unavailable with typed realm/readiness details).\n49|//\n50|// The pure core is Decide: exactly one of\n51|// launch|reattach|attach_remote|takeover_offer|parked(reason)|\n52|// refused(class). Arm order is precedence and is pinned by the\n53|// decision table: configuration, session, bootstrap idempotency,\n54|// backend identity and capability admission, fencing (activation or\n55|// restore entry), materialization, checkpoint, provider identity,\n56|// provider-auth smoke, realm readiness, profile derivation and\n57|// mapping, entrypoint, provider descriptor, then the outcome\n58|// selection (reattach, remote attach/takeover offer, launch).\n59|//\n60|// Durable state: the bootstrap binding store (binding.go) binds\n61|// (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id) to the one recorded\n62|// wrapper/child before any launch side effect under the landed\n63|// no-replace + fsync discipline with crash hooks. It never persists\n64|// or replicates a PID: identity is the AX-allocated UUIDv7 terminal\n65|// instance ID plus the binding digest. Parked decisions are authored\n66|// through sessrepo.AppendEvent under the current lease (events.go).\n67|//\n68|// Bounds: no `ax` CLI surface, no tmux/ConPTY process control, no\n69|// provider process supervision, no mesh transport, and no GUI/Keychain\n70|// broker live here. Those are modeled callers (their facts arrive as\n71|// Decide inputs) and later leaves. The mesh lease refresh of\n72|// after-restore step 2 is a caller-reported fact (Verified), not a\n73|// network call. Signature verification is caller-supplied through\n74|// terminalbackend.SignatureVerifier.\n75|package axpane","final_result":true}}}
