{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e24d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0c8-2197-71f2-b37c-575c8ab978c8"},"sequence":3969,"recorded_at":1780531400007933,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0e3-dada-7c61-b1a7-43915e4176aa"},"task_id":"01a0b0e3-dada-7c61-b1a7-43915e4176aa","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0e3-dada-7c61-b1a7-43915e4176aa","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 75-77\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-| Background caller without attested server | `Decide` → `checkRealm` → `axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable` | `TestDecideTable/refused_realm_background_no_server`, `TestDecideTypedRefusals/capability_unavailable_details`, `TestDecideTable/launch_background_attested_server` | Driven: a background caller with no attested server refuses `capability_unavailable` with typed realm/readiness details and never creates a server; an attested server launches. Incomplete typed details refuse `invalid_arguments` (`TestDecideTable/refused_realm_background_incomplete_details`). |\n-| Cached evidence never authorizes | `Realm` struct (structural) | `TestRealmCarriesNoCachedEvidence` | Driven: the `Realm` input carries exactly caller, attested-server fact, and typed details — no member accepts a cached sentinel or `managername` observation, so neither can authorize resume through any input value. |\n-| Bootstrap idempotency | `Store.Bind`, `Decide` (idempotency arm), `Run` | `TestDecideTable/refused_idempotency_mismatch`, `TestDecideTable/reattach_same_pair`, `TestBindIdenticalRetryReattaches`, `TestBindChangedOperationRefusesMismatch`, `TestBindConcurrentSameOperationReattaches`, `TestBindConcurrentChangedOperationRefuses`, `TestRunReattaches`, `TestRunConcurrentLaunchReattaches`, `TestRunIdempotencyMismatch` | Driven: a changed operation in the bootstrap window refuses `idempotency_mismatch`; an identical retry reattaches to the one recorded child (the stored receipt is authoritative); a concurrent same-operation commit reattaches while a changed-operation commit refuses. |\n+| Background caller without attested server | `Decide` → `checkRealm` → `terminalbackend.Reconcile` + `axerror.NewRealmEvidenceUnavailable` | `TestDecideTable/refused_realm_background_no_server`, `TestDecideTypedRefusals/capability_unavailable_details`, `TestDecideTable/launch_background_attested_server`, `TestDecideRealmBindingMismatchRefuses` | Driven: a background caller authorizes only through the admitted `credential_capable_execution_realm` row bound to the host binding, probed build, and current generation; without it (or with a mismatched binding/build or stale generation) it refuses `capability_unavailable` with typed details and never creates a server. Incomplete typed details refuse `invalid_arguments` (`TestDecideTable/refused_realm_background_incomplete_details`). |\n+| Cached evidence never authorizes | `Decide` → `checkRealm` + `checkSmoke` (behavioral) | `TestRealmCarriesNoCachedEvidence` | Driven: a background caller with a passing (cached) smoke record but no admitted realm row refuses; with a stale generation refuses; only the admitted row bound to the current generation, host binding, and probed build launches — no cached sentinel, `managername`, or boolean authorizes. |\n+| Bootstrap idempotency | `Store.Bind`/`Supersede`, `Decide` (windowed idempotency arm), `Run` | `TestDecideTable/refused_idempotency_mismatch`, `TestDecideRestoreChangedOperationRefuses`, `TestDecidePostWindowNewOperationLaunches`, `TestDecideTable/reattach_same_pair`, `TestBindIdenticalRetryReattaches`, `TestBindChangedOperationRefusesMismatch`, `TestBindSweepsStaleStaging`, `TestBindConcurrentSameOperationReattaches`, `TestBindConcurrentChangedOperationRefuses`, `TestRunReattaches`, `TestRunConcurrentLaunchReattaches`, `TestRunIdempotencyMismatch`, `TestRunPostWindowSupersedes` | Driven: a changed operation inside the bootstrap window (winner without a checkpoint) refuses `idempotency_mismatch` in both modes; an identical retry reattaches to the one recorded child (the stored receipt is authoritative); a concurrent same-operation commit reattaches while a changed-operation commit refuses; after the window closes (winner carries a checkpoint) a new operation supersedes and launches. Stale pre-commit staging is swept. |\n","final_result":true}}}
