{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e371","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0c8-2197-71f2-b37c-575c8ab978c8"},"sequence":4115,"recorded_at":1780531400008225,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0e4-4708-7672-964c-4cd715148ca2"},"task_id":"01a0b0e4-4708-7672-964c-4cd715148ca2","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0e4-4708-7672-964c-4cd715148ca2","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2138 line(s) above)\n2139|## Pane enforcement wrapper (`ax pane` validation core)\n2140|\n2141|[`internal/axpane`](internal/axpane) implements the validation core of the\n2142|`ax pane SESSION_ID` enforcement wrapper: the decision every managed pane runs\n2143|before launching, reattaching, offering, parking, or refusing a provider\n2144|(pinned Sections 4.B-4.D, 4.1-4.2, 5.2 Terminal Events, 7.A, and 13.1, plus the\n2145|2.4 profile authority). The pure core `Decide` returns exactly one of\n2146|`launch`, `reattach`, `attach_remote`, `takeover_offer`, `parked(reason)`, or\n2147|`refused(class)`, composing every check from a landed gate: owner epoch and\n2148|fencing from `fencing` (activation or restore entry, sealed `LeaseToken`,\n2149|parked vocabulary), materialization from `matjournal` plus checkpoint admission\n2150|from `sessckpt`/`sessrepo`, the effective profile from `sessprofile` with\n2151|`provhost` mapping refusals, provider identity from `provhost` with\n2152|`resumesmoke` evidence as a precondition, backend identity and closed\n2153|capabilities from `terminalbackend`, configuration from `config`, and refusal\n2154|shapes from `axerror`. `Run` orchestrates the adapters over the durable stores\n2155|and applies exactly the authorized effect: launch binds the bootstrap\n2156|`(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)` pair before any provider side effect,\n2157|reattach returns the one recorded child, parked and remote-offer decisions\n2158|author `session.parked` under the current lease, and refused decisions write\n2159|nothing. The bootstrap store installs under the no-replace plus fsync\n2160|discipline with crash hooks, persists no PID, and reattaches linearizably on\n2161|the commit race; a background caller without an attested server refuses\n2162|`capability_unavailable` with typed realm/readiness details, and no cached\n2163|sentinel or `managername` observation can authorize resume.\n2164|\n2165|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n2166|\n2167|```bash\n2168|go test ./internal/axpane -count=1\n2169|go test ./internal/axpane -cover -count=1\n2170|```\n2171|\n2172|Run the narrowing battery (24 narrowing mutants plus one harmless control)\n2173|with:\n2174|\n2175|```bash\n2176|PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py\n2177|```\n2178|\n2179|The harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer\n2180|through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and reports\n2181|per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1` additionally\n2182|prints the raw per-plant logs. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\n2183|attached to `TASK-260830-1geqhj`. The package adds no `ax` command, no\n2184|`doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test matrix\n2185|with its stated bounds lives in\n2186|[the task evidence map](internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md).\n2187|\n2188|## Ownership reducer properties\n2189|\n2190|The four story-pinned ownership invariants (pinned v0.6.0 Sections 2.2, 5.3,\n2191|and 13.6-13.10) hold as executable property tests over the landed production\n2192|reducers — `sessstate.Reduce` with `Compare` and the union projection,\n2193|`sessrepo.WinningLease` with `ListLeases`, and `fencing.Authorize*`:\n2194|\n2195|1. Union-order independence: every permutation of a union multiset, and every\n2196|   partition into successive unions, projects byte-identically (winner,\n2197|   conflicts, divergent-history warnings). Losing-branch evidence is a pure\n2198|   function of the union multiset: every entry below the final winner reports\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
