{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e7cb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0c8-2197-71f2-b37c-575c8ab978c8"},"sequence":4672,"recorded_at":1780531400009339,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0f3-19d5-7a22-810c-0e3abad7a868"},"task_id":"01a0b0f3-19d5-7a22-810c-0e3abad7a868","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0f3-19d5-7a22-810c-0e3abad7a868","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-78-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 40 LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check logbook format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1geqhj — ax pane enforcement wrapper validation core (first leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/axpane` — the pure `Decide` core (`launch|reattach|attach_remote|takeover_offer|parked|refused`), the `Run` orchestration over real stores, the durable bootstrap `(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)` binding store, §5.2 event authorship, and the §7.A descriptor builder. Every check composes a landed gate (`fencing`, `matjournal`, `sessckpt`/`sessrepo`, `sessprofile`, `provhost`, `resumesmoke`, `terminalbackend`, `config`, `axerror`); nothing is re-implemented. First leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\\n- F1: `fencing` launch entries refuse — not park — foreign sessions, malformed tokens, and lapsed grants, so the wrapper's `refused(lease_conflict)` rows for foreign/expired inputs compose directly; only remote/ambiguous/unverified/absent/stale ownership parks. Remote parks resolve locally to `attach_remote` (interactive + attach admitted) or `takeover_offer`, and both offers still author `session.parked` with `remote_owner`.\\n- F2: the tuple gate must precede profile mapping in arm order: `ResolveMapping` re-checks the tuple internally, so mapping-first would wear tuple refusals as `profile_mapping_unavailable`. The standalone `CheckResumeTuple` call stays as fail-fast ordering; weakening it alone is unobservable (defense in depth, stated in TRACEABILITY.md).\\n- F3: `terminalbackend.Reconcile` maps generation drift to the more specific `terminal_backend_stale_generation` (not the generic mismatch), and `create` is conferred by both `durable_disconnect` and `headless_creation` — the unproven vector must deny both. `sessckpt.Get` re-attests through `sessrepo` on every read, so checkpoint admission composes through the read path.\\n- F4: `Bind` is linearizable on the commit race via link-EEXIST re-read (same operation reattaches to the winner, changed operation refuses); the `AfterStage` hook plays the concurrent winner deterministically in tests. The store stamps `created_at` itself — scalar timestamps require ≥3 fractional digits, so `time.RFC3339Nano` (which omits trailing zeros) is not a valid stamp.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 24 narrowing mutants, all KILLED by named tests through `internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py`, plus the applied harmless SURVIVED control (25/25 rows match; per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits in the outcome tar). No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\\n- AC: 41 of 41 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via the no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n- F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\n- F2 (MEASURED BOUND): an idle stream with zero traffic does NOT self-close within one second of revocation — `serveLoop` carries no background watchdog. The next dispatch fences in milliseconds and `WatchGeneration` reports the commit; recorded as a stated bound with log evidence, not a pass. Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes likewise bounded.\\n- F3: `os/exec.Cmd.Wait` called twice hangs the second caller forever — test cleanup consumes one `Wait` channel. The 8 MiB line cap is enforced twice (framing + decode), so the oversize mutant weakens both layers in one multi-file probe (harness extended for `(file, old, new)` triples). The Structured Error schema URN is `urn:ax:schema:error`; a drift vector with the wrong URN passed for the wrong reason until the mutant survived and exposed it.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 9 new narrowing probes, all killed by named `TestHostile*` vectors (same-family ALPN, dual-layer oversize, client rebind, rpc-contracts, error-version drift, truncated-dispatch ignore, snapshot integrity, correlation, static nonce); pre-existing 26 probes re-run green (neutral passed, client-cache documented SURVIVED). Per-plant logs/tables in the outcome tar.\\n- TRACEABILITY: `AC-HOST-001` registered over 20 suite tests; new `unevidenced` bindings for 11.10.1–11.10.4 + 16.1 with honest gaps (executed lanes vs stated bounds); 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed; 11.10.5 stays unowned by design (no policy reader); digest re-pinned `e327bb08...`; report 102 cases / 61 bindings / 8 unowned / 17/487 clauses; README figures + tracecheck pins updated.\\n- AC: 7 of 7 hostile rows + 13 of 13 executed AC-HOST-001 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed. NOTE: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` replay against `origin/main e4e3e88` fails on a LOGBOOK.md rebase conflict (missing replay resolution) — orchestrator-side integration issue, worktree untouched at `244a7dc`.\\n- 2026-09-17 rev3 on `fc67abd`: pin `d3eca906…`, report 132 cases / 65 bindings / 7 unowned / 49 of 535 clauses; harness denominator 24 prior + 9 new; refresh-candidate completed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2atgj4 — property-test the ownership reducer (final leaf)\\n\\n- SCOPE: executable proofs of the four story-pinned ownership invariants\\n  (union-order independence, loser preservation, clock non-authority,\\n  zero duplicate authorized owners) over `sessstate.Reduce`/`Compare`,\\n  `sessrepo.WinningLease`/`ListLeases`, and `fencing.Authorize*`\\n  (Sections 2.2, 5.3, 13.6-13.10, v0.6.0). Final leaf of\\n  STORY-260830-1oqfec; carries the story-close traceability,\\n  README, and registry re-pin items.\\n- DEFECT (RED-first): `resolveWinner` reported each losing union lease\\n  against the transient arrival-order winner, so a loser's\\n  divergent-history evidence — even its presence — depended on union\\n  order (witness: `{R@1, A@1}` on an empty chain reports the loss in\\n  one arrival order and drops it in the other). FIX: two-pass\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 7178,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1795,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
