{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e7ff","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b0c8-2197-71f2-b37c-575c8ab978c8"},"sequence":4698,"recorded_at":1780531400009391,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"53d7abd4-2111-4f48-89d8-7ded249d4ac3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b0f3-3c6f-7253-b5c4-21dd6e48ddff"},"task_id":"01a0b0f3-3c6f-7253-b5c4-21dd6e48ddff","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b0f3-3c6f-7253-b5c4-21dd6e48ddff","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-17\n-\n-### TASK-260830-1geqhj — ax pane enforcement wrapper validation core (first leaf)\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-17\n+\n+### TASK-260830-1geqhj rev2 — ax pane rework: authority, window, closure, realm\n+- REWORKED on `888ae3d` after review-verdict-rev1 (18 findings): event authority through `fencing.AuthorizeMutation` with local-hold-only emission and the §5.7 fold gate (`sessstate.Reduce`); realm authorization through the admitted `credential_capable_execution_realm` row bound to host binding/build/generation (bare boolean removed); bootstrap window closed by the winner's `HasCheckpoint` with atomic `Supersede`; checkpoint admission bound to the winning lease and session; profile from the checkpoint closure (`DeriveForHeads`); journal source bound to the lease checkpoint; non-interactive `headless_creation` conditional; remote non-interactive parks per §4.2 step 5.\n+- F1: a park decision's stale/unverified presented token never authors — `Emit` presents the winning tuple itself, so verified local-winner parks (stale, material, checkpoint) emit while remote/unverified/ambiguous/handoff parks refuse; `Run` pre-checks local hold + foldability and parks without evidence rather than manufacturing a §5.2 collision.\n+- F2: the bootstrap window is the winner's `HasCheckpoint`, not a clock: in-window changed ops refuse `idempotency_mismatch` in both modes, post-window new ops supersede via staged rename; the `binding-*.tmp` sweep is age-gated (1 min) so a concurrent live stage is never deleted.\n+- F3: resume profile is the checkpoint closure, not the head: `Run` loads the winner's heads even when the checkpoint is not otherwise required, so a head-only or losing-lease `profile.changed` never drives launch (§2.4, §13.10).\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 35 narrowing mutants, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 36/36 with control); reviewer's RM1/RM2/RM4 survivors now killed by `TestRunTornLeasePropagates`, `TestDecideRemoteOwnerPrecedesMaterialization`, `TestDecideRestoreChangedOperationRefuses`. AC 41/41 re-derived with the six previously unfaithful rows re-pinned.\n+- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n+\n+### TASK-260830-1geqhj — ax pane enforcement wrapper validation core (first leaf)\n","final_result":true}}}
